# tests/fixtures/roster-row.captured — TWO REAL `roster-state/v1` ROWS, CAPTURED, NEVER BUILT
# (wave-01 verification-cannot-lie, S14, spec AC-25; design ledger D3).
#
# WHY A CAPTURE AND NOT AN EXPECTATION. `roster_row` (payload/scripts/lib/roster.sh) is now
# the one writer of this row, and a pin that compares the one writer against a string this
# repo also wrote is a self-comparison: both halves move together and the pin stays green
# through any drift. These two lines came off a REAL roster, written by the two production
# call sites BEFORE either of them called `roster_row` — so they are the last independent
# record of the shape the fleet's readers were built against. Reproducing them is the whole
# claim.
#
# PROVENANCE. Both lines are verbatim from the live session roster
#   .bionic/tmp/roster-c04c2d44-2eac-41af-bfef-b109aeed728a.state
# (machine-local, gitignored) of the session that dispatched S14 itself, captured
# 2026-09-06 while the pre-S14 payload was the one on disk. Both name THIS slice, which is
# why they were chosen: the rows and the change they pin have one traceable origin.
#
#   INTENDED  — `hooks/dispatch-preflight.sh`'s `ROW=` (:1822), the launch-time writer.
#               `status=intended`, no `teammate_id=`/`adopted_from=`, 18 fields.
#               tool_use_id=toolu_01VwLjtaur4XoZKv4s5rzGpU is S14's own Agent call.
#   ADOPTED   — `hooks/session-poker.sh`'s `adopt_write_row` (:1578), the resume-time writer.
#               `status=identified`, `source=adopted`, and the two fields only it writes,
#               `teammate_id=` and `adopted_from=`, 20 fields. This row is S14's own agent
#               adopted forward out of predecessor session 84f06e58 after a /clear.
#
# THE ROWS ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE. The pin drives each one through the call site that made
# it; a single captured row would leave whichever writer it did not come from unpinned, and
# the adopt writer's two extra fields are exactly the drift §RA.2 was built to catch.
#
# FORMAT. Comment lines start with `#`. Every other non-empty line is one captured row,
# byte for byte, no trailing whitespace. Readers select by `|status=`.
